#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""lab — the single CLI for a nullsilver research repo.

This is the *only* legal writer of `state.json` and `events.jsonl`. Everything the
website consumes flows through here, which is why it validates aggressively and
redacts unconditionally: the event feed is public in realtime.

Zero dependencies beyond the Python 3 standard library.

Subcommands:
    lab init                      bootstrap state.json / events.jsonl / notebooks
    lab log <type> --msg ...      append a validated, redacted event
    lab events tail [-n N]        read back the feed
    lab state get [key]           read state.json
    lab state set phase=analyze   transition (validated against the state machine)
    lab trial new <exp_id>        create a compliant trial dir, emit trial.launch
    lab trial log <dir> --data    append a record to results.jsonl
    lab trial done <dir>          close a trial, update LEDGER, emit trial.done
    lab watch start|list|check|kill|close
                                  detached watchdog for long-running work
    lab protocol freeze           snapshot PROTOCOL.md -> protocol/revNNN.md
    lab protocol activate         adopt a new revision, emit protocol.revised
    lab gate request|resolve      raise / clear a human checkpoint
    lab model [--json]            which model drives this session (requested + served)
    lab validate                  lint the whole repo against the contract
    lab format show|sync|version  the output-format contract for consumers
"""
